{"version":1,"slug":"Oliiveboardd__Quant_Super_Prac__SSC_Super_Practice_Percentage_23","path":"Oliiveboardd/Quant Super Prac/SSC_Super_Practice_Percentage_23.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Oliiveboardd","category":"Quant Super Prac","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the percent change in the area of a triangle if the height of the triangle is increased by 20% and the base is decreased by 8%?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 20% &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; 8% &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">11.8 %</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11.8 %</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10.4 %</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10.4 %</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12.6 %</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12.6 %</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9.3 %</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9.3 %</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The height of triangle = h cm</p><p>Base of triangle = b cm</p><p>Original area of triangle = &frac12; *b*h</p><p>New height of triangle = 1.2*h</p><p>New base of triangle = 0.92*b</p><p>New area of triangle = (&frac12;) * 1.2*h*0.92*b = 0.552 *b*h</p><p>Required percentage = {[(0.552*b*h)  -  (0.5*b*h)] /(0.5*b*h)]} *100</p><p>= (0.052 *100) / 0.5</p><p>= 10.4 % </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Sum of two numbers is 144. If larger number is increased by 30% and the smaller number is decreased by 30%, then their difference become 75.2. Find 25% of the smaller number. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 144 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 75.2 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 25% &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19.5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19.5</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers are a (larger) and b (smaller). </p><p>a + b = 144 =&gt; a = 144  -  b </p><p>And (100 + 30)% of a  -  (100  -  30)% of b = 75.2</p><p>13a  -  7b = 752 =&gt; a = (752 + 7b)/13 </p><p>Now, 144  -  b = (752 + 7b)/13</p><p>1872  -  13b = 752 + 7b </p><p>20b = 1120</p><p>b = 56</p><p>Therefore, 25% of b = 25% of 56 = <b>14</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If 80% of 10 times of number is subtracted from the square of the number then it is increased by 1100% of itself. Find half of the number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; 10 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 80% &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2310;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1100% &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">21</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the number be n.</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>  -  0.80(10n) = 12n</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>  -  8n = 12n</p><p>n  -  8 = 12</p><p>n = 20</p><p>So, half of the number = 10</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Per capita water requirement in a small town is 120 litres/person. The population of the town is estimated to grow at a rate of 10% per year. If, the current population of the town is 45000, how much water per day will be required to meet the demand 3 years from now?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; 120 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2348;&#2366;&#2342;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367;, &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 45000 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 3 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6587.4 kilo litres/day</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6587.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8587.4 kilo litres/day</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8587.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6187.4 kilo litres/day</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6187.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7187.4 kilo litres/day</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7187.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=448 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20559/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=432 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20559/image010.png\"></p><p>Water demand 3 years later for the increased population = 59895  X  120 = 7187400 litres = 7187.4 kilo litres/day</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In an exam, Reeta got 5% marks more than passing marks and Veena got 8% marks less than passing marks. Marks obtained by Reeta and Veena are 120 and 68 respectively. Find the passing marks of the exam. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 5% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 8% &#2325;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 120 &#2324;&#2352; 68 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">50</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">200</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let maximum marks = m</p><p>Passing marks = p</p><p>p + 5% of m = 120 -----(1)</p><p>p  -  8% of m = 68 -------(2)</p><p>On solving eqn (1) and (2) -----</p><p>5% of m + 8% of m = 52</p><p>m = 52*100/13 = 400</p><p>p = 100</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>60% of the villagers are illiterate from which 80% are female. Total males in the village are 40%. What percentage of villagers are literate males?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>60% &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368;&#2339; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 80% &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 40% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368;&#2339; &#2360;&#2366;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">28%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16%</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let total number of villagers = 100</p><p>Illiterate villagers = 60% of 100 = 60</p><p>Illiterate females = 60 * 80/100 = 48</p><p>Illiterate males = 60  -  48 = 12</p><p>Total number of males = 40% of 100 = 40</p><p>Number of literate male employees = 40  -  12 = 28</p><p>Required percentage = 28/100 * 100 = 28%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A student got 112 marks in English, 102 marks in Hindi, 98 marks in Biology, and 88 marks in Maths. If the maximum marks of each subject are 120, then find the overall percentage of marks get.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 112 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 102 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;, &#2332;&#2368;&#2357; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 98 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2339;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 88 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 120 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">81.24%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">81.24%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">83.33%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">83.33%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">85.15%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">85.15%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">87.66%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">87.66%</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total marks = 112 + 102 + 98 + 88</p><p>= 400</p><p>Hence, the required percentage = 83.33%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A number is multiplied by 5/8 instead of 2/5. What is the percentage error in the calculation? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; 2/5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 5/8 &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2369;&#2335;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">56.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">56.25%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">64.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64.25%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60.25%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">58.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">58.25%</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the number be x.</p><p>Wrong value = 5x/8</p><p>Corrected value = 2x/5</p><p>Hence, the required percentage = [(5x/8  -  2x/5) * 100]/ (2x/5)</p><p>= (9x/40 * 100)/ (2x/5)</p><p>= 56.25% </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The length and breadth of a rectangle are increased by 25% and 10% respectively. Find the percentage change in its area. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 25% &#2324;&#2352; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">32.5%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32.5%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">37.5%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">37.5%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25.5%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25.5%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27.5%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27.5%</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The percentage change in its area = 25 + 10 + 25 * 10/100 = 37.5%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In an election held between two candidates, 15% of the voters did not cast their votes. 12% of the remaining voters are invalid. Total number of voters is 1500 and the losing candidate receive 282 votes. Find the number of votes received by winning candidate.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 15% &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2404; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 12% &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2309;&#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 1500 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 282 &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">630</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">630</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">840</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">840</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">750</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">750</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">720</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">720</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Total votes = 1500</p><p>Number of voters who did not cast = 15% of 1500 = 225</p><p>Remaining voters = 85% of 1500 = 1275</p><p>Invalid voters = 12% of 1275 = 153</p><p>Valid voters = 1275  -  153 = 1122</p><p>Votes received by winning candidates = 1122  -  282 = 840</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In an election, 25% of the registered voters did not vote, and 90 voters submitted blank ballot papers. There were only two candidates: Shivani and Juhi. Shivani, the winner, received support from 62% of all registered voters and secured 74668 more votes than Juhi. Determine the total number of registered voters.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2346;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 25% &#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2324;&#2352; 90 &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2350;&#2340;&#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2342;&#2379; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;: &#2358;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2370;&#2361;&#2368;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2358;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 62% &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2332;&#2370;&#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; 74668 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2346;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">142400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">142400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">138000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">138000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">152200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">152200</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">141400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">141400</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the total number of voters be V.</p><p>75% of voters cast their votes.</p><p>Total votes cast = 0.75 V</p><p>Shivani's votes = 0.62 V</p><p>Juhi's votes = 0.62V  -  74668</p><p>Total votes cast = Shivani's votes + Juhi's votes + Blank votes</p><p>0.75V = 0.62V + (0.62V  -  74668) + 90</p><p>0.49V = 74578</p><p>V = 152200</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In an election contested between two candidates, 12% of the registered voters abstained from voting, and 100 votes were marked invalid. The candidate who won secured 55% of the total votes registered and achieved victory with a margin of 9670 votes. What was the total number of registered voters?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2346;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 12% &#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2361;&#2375;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 100 &#2357;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2328;&#2379;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 55% &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 9670 &#2357;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340; &#2361;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; &#8203;&#8203;&#2346;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">43500</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">43500</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">45500</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45500</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">34200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34200</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">52100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">52100</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let total enrolled voters = x</p><p>Total votes cast = 0.88x</p><p>Total valid votes = 0.88x - 100</p><p>Winner's votes = 0.55x</p><p>Loser's votes = Winner's votes - 9670</p><p>0.55x - (0.88x - 100 - 0.55x) = 9670</p><p>0.55x  -  0.33x + 100 = 9670</p><p>0.22x = 9570</p><p>x = 43500</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The cost of milk per litre is increased by 45%. By what percentage must Chikki reduce his consumption of milk so as not to increase his expenditure? (correct up to two decimal places).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 45% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2346;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2344; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2375;? (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">40.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40.25%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28.28%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28.28%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">31.03%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31.03%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">35.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">35.25%</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the original cost price be Rs. 100/litre</p><p>And the new cost price be Rs. 145/litre</p><p>Increase in expenditure = Rs. 45</p><p>Consumption of milk should decrease by 45/145 * 100 = 31.03%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Ananya spends 70% of her income. Her income increases by 25% and her expenditure increases by 20%. What is the percentage increase in her savings?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 70% &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 25% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">36.67%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36.67%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40.25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40.25%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">45.12%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45.12%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15.67%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15.67%</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the income of Ananya = Rs. 100</p><p>Expenditure = Rs. 70</p><p>Savings = Rs. 30</p><p>New income = 100 * 125/100 = Rs. 125</p><p>New expenditure = 70 * 120/100 = Rs. 84</p><p>New savings = 125  -  84 = Rs. 41</p><p>Required percentage increase = (41  -  30)/30 * 100 = 36.67%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>30% of Yash's income is equal to 21% of Rita's income. If income of Yash got increased by Rs. 1000 and Rita's income did not change, the ratio of income of Yash to that of Rita become 3 : 4. Find the income of Rita.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 30% &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; 21% &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2351;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3 : 4 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 30000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 30000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 20000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 20000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 22000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 22000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 25000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 25000</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>30% of Yash = 21% of Rita</p><p>10 * Yash = 7 * Rita</p><p>Yash/Rita = 7/10</p><p>let income of Yash and Rita be 7a and 10a respectively,</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(7a + 1000)/10a = 3/4</p><p>14a + 2000 = 15a</p><p>a = 2000</p><p>Income of Rita = 10 * 2000 = Rs. 20000</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A 12% reduction in the cost price of a commodity allows a shopkeeper to buy 18 kg more for &#8377;7392 than he could earlier. To achieve a profit of 40% on the original cost price, at what price per kg should the commodity be sold?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 12% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; 7392 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 40% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 72.6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 72.6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 54.8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 54.8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 78.4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 78.4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 69.8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 69.8</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the original cost price be Rs. x/kg</p><p>New CP per kg = x  -  12% of x</p><p>New CP per kg = x  -  0.12x = 0.88x</p><p>Quantity purchased at new CP = 7392/0.88x</p><p>Quantity purchased at original CP = 7392/x</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(7392/0.88x)  -  (7392/x) = 18</p><p>7392 * 0.12/0.88x = 18</p><p>x = 56</p><p>Original cost price = Rs. 56/kg</p><p>Profit = 40% of 56 = Rs. 22.4</p><p>SP = CP + Profit</p><p>=&gt; 56 + 22.4 = Rs. 78.4</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Last year, Sapna's monthly salary was Rs. 15200 and Ritika's monthly salary was Rs. 16,000. This year, Sapna's monthly salary is Rs. 18240 while Ritika's monthly salary is Rs. 20000. If the percentage increase in Ritika's monthly salary this year over her monthly salary last year is denoted by a%, and the percentage increase in Sapna's monthly salary this year over her monthly salary last year is denoted by b%, then what is the value of [(a  -  b)/b * 100]%?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; 15200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; 16,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; 18240 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2352;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; 20000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2352;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; a% &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; b% &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; [(a - b)/b * 100]% &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">34%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">45%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28%</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Ritika's percentage increase = a%</p><p>a = (20000  -  16000)/16000 * 100 = 25%</p><p>Sapna's percentage increase = b%</p><p>b = (18240  -  15200)/15200 * 100 = 20%</p><p>Required value = (25  -  20)/20 * 100 = 25%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the production of car three types of cost are involved. Cost of raw materials, expenditure on labour and miscellaneous costs. Ratio of expenditure on these costs in a particular year is 4 : 3 : 2 respectively. In the next year cost of raw material increased by 10%, expenditure on labour increased by 8% and miscellaneous cost decreased by 5%. Find the percentage rise in the cost of car?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340;, &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2367;&#2343; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2344; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4: 3: 2 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;, &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; 8% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2367;&#2343; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; 5% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2310;&#2312;&#2404; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5%</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Cost of raw material = 4x</p><p>Expenditure costs = 3x</p><p>Miscellaneous costs = 2x</p><p>Total cost = 4x + 3x + 2x = 9x</p><p>Amount = (4x * 110) / 100 + (3x * 108) / 100 + (2x * 95) / 100</p><p>= 9.54x</p><p>Percentage rise = (9.54x  -  9x) / 9x * 100 = 6%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If a person spends 35% of his monthly income on his rent, 20% of the rest of the income on food, 25% of the remaining income on shopping, and he saves the remaining Rs. 1950, then find the monthly income.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 35% &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 20% &#2349;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 25% &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2361; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2352;&#2369;.1950 &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 5400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 5400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 5000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 5000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 6400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 6400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 7200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 7200</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the income be '100'.</p><p><img width=463 height=128 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24801/image004.jpg\" ></p><p>39 = Rs. 1950 </p><p>1 = 50 </p><p>Hence, monthly income = 50 * 100 = Rs. 5000 </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Faizal donates every year 9% of her annual salary into a charity. If his annual salary is Rs. 450000, then what is the annual contribution into the charity?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2347;&#2376;&#2332;&#2364;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2376;&#2354;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 9% &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2344; 450000 &#2352;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 41600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 41600</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 40500</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 40500</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 42500</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 42500</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 45500</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 45500</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>His annual salary is Rs. 450000,</p><p>So, his annual contribution into the charity = 450000 * 9/100 = Rs. 40500</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}